From: Richard T. Carback III <rick.carback@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: core: Add ctrl_retries to retry control transfers after transaction errors

On the ASUS Ascent QN10, a KVM hub (05e3:0610) behind the internal
Genesys hub fails about 10% of control transfers with -EPROTO after the
xHCI controller's own retries. The failures are independent: a second
try fails about 16% of the time, and three retries leave none in 3000
requests. Hub status reads and descriptor reads then fail, and the hub
driver resets or drops the KVM. Bulk and interrupt endpoints already get
xHCI soft retries; control transfers do not.

Add the usbcore.ctrl_retries parameter (default 0). usb_control_msg()
retries a request that failed with -EPROTO or -EILSEQ, from the SETUP
stage, up to ctrl_retries times.

Local test patch for the QN10 7.4-rc1 kernel build.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/core/message.c b/drivers/usb/core/message.c
index a738d03c2..e551dc044 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/core/message.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/message.c
@@ -27,6 +27,18 @@
 
 static void cancel_async_set_config(struct usb_device *udev);
 
+/*
+ * A marginal link (for example a hub behind a hub) can fail a control
+ * transfer with a transaction error even after the host controller's own
+ * retries. Bulk and interrupt endpoints get more retries from the HCD
+ * (xHCI soft retry), control transfers do not. Retry the whole request
+ * from the SETUP stage up to ctrl_retries times.
+ */
+static unsigned int ctrl_retries;
+module_param(ctrl_retries, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(ctrl_retries,
+		 "retries for a control message that fails with -EPROTO or -EILSEQ (default 0)");
+
 struct api_context {
 	struct completion	done;
 	int			status;
@@ -152,6 +164,7 @@ int usb_control_msg(struct usb_device *dev, unsigned int pipe, __u8 request,
 		    __u16 size, int timeout)
 {
 	struct usb_ctrlrequest *dr;
+	unsigned int tries;
 	int ret;
 
 	dr = kmalloc_obj(struct usb_ctrlrequest, GFP_NOIO);
@@ -164,7 +177,14 @@ int usb_control_msg(struct usb_device *dev, unsigned int pipe, __u8 request,
 	dr->wIndex = cpu_to_le16(index);
 	dr->wLength = cpu_to_le16(size);
 
-	ret = usb_internal_control_msg(dev, pipe, dr, data, size, timeout);
+	for (tries = 0;; tries++) {
+		ret = usb_internal_control_msg(dev, pipe, dr, data, size, timeout);
+		if ((ret != -EPROTO && ret != -EILSEQ) ||
+		    tries >= READ_ONCE(ctrl_retries))
+			break;
+		dev_dbg(&dev->dev, "control request %02x/%02x failed (%d), retry %u\n",
+			requesttype, request, ret, tries + 1);
+	}
 
 	/* Linger a bit, prior to the next control message. */
 	if (dev->quirks & USB_QUIRK_DELAY_CTRL_MSG)
